WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.761
Perda sat near a big tree, thinking.

2
00:00:02.762 --> 00:00:07.769
A few hours had passed since she, Fala, Darb, and Gliss had joined the rebels.

3
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.369
But to Perda it felt like a few years.

4
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:15.093
Nothing was happening except lots of talking. And Zann still hadn't shown up.

5
00:00:15.094 --> 00:00:18.683
What if he hadn't been able to escape from the palace after that fall?

6
00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:21.264
Gliss and Darb wandered over to her.

7
00:00:21.265 --> 00:00:24.778
"What are the adults talking about now?" Perda asked.

8
00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:29.281
Darb sat down and gave Zing a pat. "Same stuff," he replied.

9
00:00:29.282 --> 00:00:34.707
"Half of them want to try Fala's plan to ride our dragons to the fortress and free Morb's prisoners.

10
00:00:34.708 --> 00:00:40.204
The others think we should just stay here and spy on Morb until we know what he's planning to do next.

11
00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:45.107
They say that until we know Morb's plans, there's no point in doing anything."

12
00:00:45.108 --> 00:00:47.322
Perda looked at the group of adults.

13
00:00:47.323 --> 00:00:51.157
Fala was still huddled with her friend Shem and some of the rebel leaders.

14
00:00:51.158 --> 00:00:55.408
"Seems like the only thing these rebels do is talk," Perda said.

15
00:00:55.409 --> 00:00:59.417
Gliss glanced up at the patch of sky that was visible through the trees.

16
00:00:59.418 --> 00:01:02.024
"It'll be getting dark soon," she said.

17
00:01:02.025 --> 00:01:05.938
"We should check the meeting spot again to see if Zann's there yet."

18
00:01:05.939 --> 00:01:13.845
A whisper of excitement ran through the camp as a spy fly buzzed into the clearing and headed for Vig, the leader of the rebel group.

19
00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:16.889
He was a tall, lean man with droopy eyes.

20
00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:23.004
"What's the spy fly showing you, Vig?" someone asked after the fly had burrowed into Vig's ear.

21
00:01:23.005 --> 00:01:28.595
Perda held her breath; the rebel leader closed his eyes to focus on the spy fly's message.

22
00:01:28.596 --> 00:01:31.653
"It found Morb," Vig said after a moment.

23
00:01:31.654 --> 00:01:37.346
"I'm not sure this place is the palace though—I also see a dungeon.

24
00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:40.915
I've never heard of a dungeon at the palace."

25
00:01:40.916 --> 00:01:45.548
"There is one," said a woman. "It dates back to the Old Times.

26
00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:50.734
But our king and queen have never imprisoned people—they just use it for storage."

27
00:01:50.735 --> 00:01:57.209
"Not anymore." Vig closed his eyes again. "It's full of Red prisoners now."

28
00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:01.823
Perda gasped. "Did Morb recapture the people we rescued from the zoo?"

29
00:02:01.824 --> 00:02:08.834
"I don't think so," said Vig. "I see Boz. The king and queen are there too."

30
00:02:08.835 --> 00:02:11.743
There were murmurs of confusion from all around.

31
00:02:11.744 --> 00:02:16.263
"Are you sure you're seeing the palace and not Morb's fortress?" Fala asked.

32
00:02:16.264 --> 00:02:19.839
Vig nodded grimly as the spy fly flew out of his ear.

33
00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:26.385
"I'm sure. It looks like Morb somehow transported all of his prisoners to First City."

34
00:02:26.386 --> 00:02:32.236
Vig gulped. "I can't imagine how much magic that must have taken."

35
00:02:32.237 --> 00:02:37.644
Shem spoke up. "We need to go back to the palace and rescue those prisoners."

36
00:02:37.645 --> 00:02:40.980
"How do you propose to do that?" asked a woman.

37
00:02:40.981 --> 00:02:44.758
"We must attack Morb at once," said someone else.

38
00:02:44.759 --> 00:02:49.175
"Morb is much too powerful," muttered an older man.

39
00:02:49.176 --> 00:02:54.045
The adults continued to argue about what to do next. Perda had heard enough.

40
00:02:54.046 --> 00:02:57.970
"Let's go check for Zann," Perda whispered to Gliss and Darb.

41
00:02:57.971 --> 00:03:02.271
The three of them slipped away from the clearing, with Zing flying just overhead.

42
00:03:02.272 --> 00:03:07.140
"I wonder if Zann knows that Boz is in the palace now," Darb said as they walked.

43
00:03:07.141 --> 00:03:11.401
"Do you think my parents are there too?" Gliss sounded anxious.

44
00:03:11.402 --> 00:03:16.745
"Probably," Perda said. "But why would Morb bring all those Reds to First City?

45
00:03:16.746 --> 00:03:20.325
Isn't he worried that they'll be easier to rescue there?"

46
00:03:20.326 --> 00:03:26.153
"I doubt it. Morb thinks he'll be able to control everyone's magic soon," Darb pointed out.

47
00:03:26.154 --> 00:03:31.781
By then they had reached the clearing, where the two cloud gliders grazed in the tall grass.

48
00:03:31.782 --> 00:03:35.572
Light from the setting sun shimmered gently across their scales.

49
00:03:35.573 --> 00:03:39.468
"Nobody's here except the dragons," Gliss said.

50
00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:43.216
Perda's heart sank. "I hope Zann is okay."

51
00:03:43.217 --> 00:03:46.329
"I'm sure he's fine," said Gliss.

52
00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:50.466
"Yeah," said Darb, "Zann knows how to take care of himself.

53
00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.466
He'll find a way out of the palace."

54
00:03:52.467 --> 00:04:00.230
Perda wasn't reassured. "Maybe we can convince the rebels to send out a search party tomorrow morning to look for Zann."

55
00:04:00.231 --> 00:04:04.633
Just then a twig snapped as a figure walked into the clearing.

56
00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:11.668
"You don't need to send out a search party," said a familiar voice. "I'm right here!"

57
00:04:11.669 --> 00:04:17.385
After checking on the prisoners in the dungeon, Morb returned to the upstairs room to await Wyssa.

58
00:04:17.386 --> 00:04:25.503
"Where is she?" he muttered. "It's bad enough she protected Boz's grandson. Now she keeps me waiting!"

59
00:04:25.504 --> 00:04:32.298
Morb needed Wyssa for one last, very important errand—to fetch a batch of blue leeches.

60
00:04:32.299 --> 00:04:38.423
Then his machine would be fully operational, and he would no longer have to rely on the old woman.

61
00:04:38.424 --> 00:04:41.996
It was past nightfall, and Wyssa still hadn't arrived.

62
00:04:41.997 --> 00:04:48.253
Morb grew furious. "This is ridiculous! Where is she?"

63
00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:51.065
He waved a hand and called up the Directory.

64
00:04:51.066 --> 00:04:55.380
"Wyssa!" he commanded when the translucent screen appeared before him.

65
00:04:55.381 --> 00:05:01.132
Wyssa's entry slowly formed. It was short, and many of the sections were blank.

66
00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:06.102
There was a notation at the top: "No longer a resident of Magica."

67
00:05:06.103 --> 00:05:09.178
"There must be some mistake," Morb grumbled.

68
00:05:09.179 --> 00:05:15.478
He glared at the Directory and cleared his throat. "Provide details," he ordered loudly.

69
00:05:15.479 --> 00:05:22.368
"Individual not currently in Magica. No possessions of individual currently in Magica.

70
00:05:22.369 --> 00:05:26.777
Individual is presumed to be permanently off-world."

71
00:05:26.778 --> 00:05:34.236
"No!" Morb gnashed his teeth. In a fit of rage, he blasted a hole in the wall.

72
00:05:34.237 --> 00:05:38.361
"Without those leeches, my machine is useless!"

73
00:05:38.362 --> 00:05:41.188
Morb stepped over to look out the big hole.

74
00:05:41.189 --> 00:05:44.242
Slib was hurrying past in the courtyard below.

75
00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:48.242
Morb's fury faded and was replaced by determination.

76
00:05:48.243 --> 00:05:51.553
Wyssa was gone, but maybe Morb didn't need her.

77
00:05:51.554 --> 00:06:00.555
After all, he was the king, and he had absolute authority over his subjects.

